  "progress.ofPlots": "{percent} of the plots",
  "progress.chartTitle": "Plots submitted over time",
  "progress.chartExplain": "The line is the number of plots submitted by the end of each day, counting the plots submitted now on the day they were first submitted; the table also gives how many were first submitted each day. Only first assessments count: quality checks and plots in no plot file do not. Days are those of your time zone, {zone}, and the last 90 days are shown, from the day before the first submission.\n\nA plot counts once it reaches the server: plots that sync late are added to the day they were first submitted, so a past day can grow. A plot that is no longer submitted leaves the line. Point at a day, or select the chart and use the arrow keys, to read its figures; “Table” lists every day, newest first. A dashed line marks the target when there is a deadline or a target set in Settings.",
  "progress.chartExplain.short": "Plots submitted by the end of each day, in your time zone. Quality checks are not counted.",
  "progress.chartLabel": "Plots submitted in total, from {from} to {to}. The table view gives every day.",
  "progress.chartKeys": "Use the left and right arrow keys to go from day to day.",
  "progress.point": "{date}: {total} plots submitted in total, {day} submitted that day",
  "progress.targetLine": "Target: {n}",
  "progress.dayColumn": "Day",
  "progress.dayCount": "Submitted that day",
  "progress.totalCount": "Submitted in total",
  "progress.forecastTitle": "When will it be done?",
  "progress.forecastTitle.more": "The target is the number of plots set in the Settings tab or, when none is set, every plot given to someone; the plots left are the target minus the plots submitted now. The pace is the plots first submitted in the last 14 days, today included, divided by 14 (by fewer days when the first plot was submitted less than 14 days ago). The plots left divided by the pace, rounded up, give the days left and the end date.\n\nWith a deadline, the plots a day needed are the plots left divided by the days until it, the deadline day included. A coordinator sets the deadline and the target under Progress in the Settings tab; the forecast changes at the next reload. The pace follows the last 14 days only, so a slow or busy week moves the date a lot.",
  "progress.forecastTarget": "Target: {target} plots, every plot given to someone.",
