  "attention.storageTitle": "Space almost full",
  "attention.storageOverTitle": "No space left",
  "attention.oldFileTitle": "Old project file",
  "attention.oldFile": "{count} people have the project file from before it was last replaced (only people who hold plots or have synced are counted). Collect Earth does not get the new one by itself.\n\nFor each of them, open their page in People and press “Make a link for the new project file”. Send the link to that person only: it is shown once and works for a week. In Collect Earth they choose File → Join cloud project..., paste it and press “Log in” with their account, not Register; Collect Earth downloads the project file as it is now and restarts. The link is not used up and their role does not change. Once they have it, they leave this list at the next reload.",
  "attention.oldFile.short": "{count} people have the project file from before it was replaced: on their pages in People, make them new links.",
  "attention.oldFileOne": "One person has the project file from before it was last replaced (only people who hold plots or have synced are counted). Collect Earth does not get the new one by itself.\n\nOpen their page in People and press “Make a link for the new project file”. Send the link to that person only: it is shown once and works for a week. In Collect Earth they choose File → Join cloud project..., paste it and press “Log in” with their account, not Register; Collect Earth downloads the project file as it is now and restarts. The link is not used up and their role does not change. Once they have it, this item goes away at the next reload.",
  "attention.oldFileOne.short": "One person has the project file from before it was replaced: on their page in People, make them a new link.",
  "attention.oldCeTitle": "Old Collect Earth",
  "attention.oldCe": "{count} people use a Collect Earth older than the one that hides which plots are quality checks. Ask them to update it.",
  "attention.oldCeOne": "One person uses a Collect Earth older than the one that hides which plots are quality checks. Ask them to update it.",
