  "attention.unknownCeOne": "For one person, the version of Collect Earth could not be told yet.",
  "progressSettings.title": "Progress",
  "progressSettings.intro": "For the forecast on the Progress tab, and to find people who have gone quiet (no sync and no plot download).",
  "progressSettings.deadline": "Deadline (optional)",
  "progressSettings.deadlineHelp": "The last day of the collection.",
  "progressSettings.deadlinePast": "That day has passed: the Progress tab will count the collection as late. Check the year.",
  "progressSettings.target": "Target in plots (optional)",
  "progressSettings.targetHelp": "Leave it empty to count every plot given to someone.",
  "progressSettings.targetHelp.more": "The forecast on the Progress tab counts the plots left: the target minus the plots already submitted, or, with no target, every plot given to someone minus those submitted. It divides them by the pace, the plots first submitted per day over the last 14 days (or since the first plot, in a younger collection), to give the day the collection should end; with no plot in those days, no day is given. With a deadline, it also says how many plots a day are needed to finish in time, the deadline day included.\n\nSet a target when only part of the plots given out must be done, or when more plots will be given later. The progress links below show the same forecast.",
  "progressSettings.quietDays": "Quiet after this many days",
  "progressSettings.quietDaysHelp": "Someone is quiet when they still have plots to do (their own plots or checks given to them) and more than this many days have passed since their last sync or plot download, whichever came later. Type a whole number from 1 to 365 and press “Save”; until you change it, it is 3. Someone who has never synced nor downloaded plots is not called quiet: they are listed under “Plots not downloaded”. A disabled account is never quiet.\n\nQuiet people are named on the Progress tab, marked on the People tab (orange after this many days, red after twice as many) and in the weekly summary of the coordinators who asked for it. Choose a little more than the usual gap between two working days of your team: too low, and people who sync once a week show as quiet.",
  "progressSettings.quietDaysHelp.short": "Days without a sync or plot download before someone shows as quiet.",
  "progressSettings.badDeadline": "Write a date, or leave it empty.",
  "progressSettings.badTarget": "A whole number from 1 to 10,000,000, or empty.",
  "progressSettings.badQuiet": "A whole number from 1 to 365.",
  "progressSettings.saved": "The progress settings are saved.",
