  "overview.stepsDone": "{done} of {total} steps done",
  "overview.allDone": "All steps done. Follow the collection in the Progress tab.",
  "overview.plots": "Plots",
  "overview.submitted": "Submitted records, quality checks included",
  "overview.plotFiles": "Plot files",
  "overview.people": "People",
  "overview.byPerson": "Progress of each person",
  "overview.byPerson.more": "One row for each name plots were sent under from Collect Earth, in alphabetical order. “Saved” counts all of that person's plots the server has, finished or not; “Submitted”, those they submitted. Quality checks they made count in both, and deleted plots in neither. “Last activity” is the latest time one of their plots was changed, in your time zone.\n\nA person with many saved but few submitted plots may still have plots to finish and submit. The figures are those of when you opened this page: reload it to see newer ones.",
  "overview.person": "Person",
  "overview.submittedCol": "Submitted",
  "overview.savedCol": "Saved",
  "overview.lastActivity": "Last activity",
  "overview.unknownPerson": "(no name)",
  "overview.noData": "Nobody has sent plots yet. They appear here as soon as people submit plots in Collect Earth.",
  "storage.used": "Space used: {used} of {limit}",
  "storage.usedNoLimit": "Space used: {used}",
  "storage.explain": "This counts the project file, the plot files and the plots collected.",
  "storage.explain.more": "The space limit is the same for every project of this server and is set by the server administrator; without a limit, only the space used is shown. Uploading a project file, or a plot file with the same name as one already here, replaces the old one, so only the new one counts.\n\nFrom 90 % of the limit a warning appears. Over the limit, the project file and plot files can no longer be uploaded, but the plots people send from Collect Earth are always received and kept. Ask the server administrator for more space before you reach it.",
  "storage.nearlyFull": "This project has almost no space left. Plots from collectors are always received, but soon you will not be able to upload a project file or plot files. Ask the server administrator for more space.",
  "storage.over": "This project uses more space than it is allowed. Plots from collectors are still received and kept, but you cannot upload a project file or plot files. Ask the server administrator for more space.",

  "step.done": "Done",
  "step.todo": "To do",
  "step.projectFile.title": "Upload the project file",
  "step.projectFile.help": "The .cep file of your survey, made in Collect Earth. Collectors receive it when they join.",
  "step.projectFile.help.more": "The project file holds your survey: the questions and the map settings. Export it from Collect Earth as a .cep file and drop it on the Project file tab. The step is done once a project file is uploaded.\n\nUpload it before you invite people and before anyone collects. People who join get the version uploaded at that moment; a new version reaches those who joined before only through a new link, made on each person's page in People. While no data has been collected, the server also adds a hidden 'round' to the survey so that quality checks are blind; once data has been collected, it leaves the survey as it is.",
  "step.projectFile.action": "Upload",
  "step.plotFiles.title": "Add plot files",
  "step.plotFiles.help": "CSV files with the plots to collect.",
  "step.plotFiles.action": "Add plot files",
  "step.invite.title": "Invite people",
  "step.invite.help": "Make an invitation link and send it to the people who will collect.",
  "step.invite.help.more": "On the People tab, choose the role they join as (Collector unless you change it), how many people can use the link (10) and how long it works (1 month), then press “Make the invitation link”. Copy the link at once: it is shown only once. Send it by email or chat; the person opens Collect Earth, chooses File → Join cloud project..., pastes it and chooses a username and a password, and Collect Earth downloads the project.\n\nThe step is done once someone else is in the project or a link is still open. “Stop this link”, under “Invitation links still open”, stops a link that should not be used any more.",
  "step.invite.action": "Invite people",
  "step.assign.title": "Choose who collects each plot file",
  "step.assign.help": "Each person receives only the plot files you give them.",
  "step.assign.help.more": "On the Plot files tab, in “Who collects each file”, tick a box to give a whole file to a person and press “Save”: nothing changes for anyone before you save. To share a file's plots out between several people instead, use “Divide plots” in the list of files.\n\nIn Collect Earth, each person finds their plot files under Settings → “Project”; if Collect Earth was already open, “Refresh assignments” there updates the list, and they choose the file and press “Apply”. The dashboard sends them no message, so tell them when their plots are ready.",
  "step.assign.action": "Choose",
  "step.progress.title": "Follow the progress",
  "step.progress.help": "Plots arrive here as people submit them in Collect Earth.",
  "step.progress.action": "See the data",

