  "plots.gridTitle": "Who collects each file",
  "plots.gridHelp": "Tick a box to give a file to a person. Each person receives only the files ticked for them.",
  "plots.gridHelp.more": "Each row is a plot file, each column a person (collectors and reviewers first, coordinators last). A ticked box gives that person the whole file: every plot in it. Tick the boxes, then press “Save”: nothing changes for anyone before you save, and ticks not saved are lost when you leave the page.\n\nTick a file for more than one person only if each of them should collect all of its plots: they would then assess the same plots twice. To share a file's plots out between people, use “Divide plots” in the list above; a divided file shows a label here instead of boxes and is changed on its own page.",
  "plots.gridNeedsPeople": "Invite people first, then come back here to give them plot files.",
  "plots.assignLabel": "{person} collects {file}",
  "plots.saveAssign": "Save",
  "plots.unsaved": "You have changes that are not saved yet.",
  "plots.assignSaved": "Saved. In Collect Earth, each person finds the plot files you gave them under Settings → “Project”, in “Assigned plot file”. If Collect Earth was already open, “Refresh assignments” there updates the list; they choose the file and press “Apply”.\n\nThe dashboard sends them no message, so tell them when a new file is ready. A file you untick is no longer among that person's assigned files after their next refresh; the records they already submitted on it stay in the project.",
  "plots.assignSaved.short": "Saved. In Collect Earth, each person finds their plot files under Settings → “Project”.",

