  "divide.columnHelp": "Columns with more than 200 different values cannot be used.",
  "divide.value": "Value",
  "divide.valuePeople": "Who collects",
  "divide.valuePeopleLabel": "Who collects the plots with {value}",
  "divide.emptyValue": "(empty)",
  "divide.nobody": "Nobody",
  "divide.inTurn": "Give every value to one person, in turn",
  "divide.inTurnHelp": "Each value goes to one collector, taking them in turn. You can change it afterwards.",
  "divide.unassignedHint": "Plots with a value that nobody collects are not given to anyone.",
  "divide.checkTitle": "Quality check",
  "divide.checkTitle.more": "Each person's copies go to one other person of the division: the share you type, rounded up, of that person's plots, spread through their list. That person assesses them as a check, and the Quality tab shows the plots where the two answers differ. Nobody gets a copy of a plot they collect.\n\nCopies are extra work: a person's “Plots” count includes them, and “Copies to compare” says how many. It needs at least two people. A plot that already has a copy (someone submitted its check) keeps it, and it counts towards the share.",
  "divide.checkSwitch": "Also give some plots to a second person, to compare answers",
  "divide.checkPercent": "Share of each person's plots (%)",
  "divide.checkPercentHelp": "From 5 to 50. The Quality tab shows the plots where the two answers differ.",
  "divide.preview": "Preview",
  "divide.apply": "Apply",
  "divide.applyNote": "“Preview” shows how many plots and copies to compare each person would get, and how many plots would go to nobody; it saves nothing. “Apply” replaces the file's current division, plots moved by hand included; collectors get the new list when they next refresh in Collect Earth. With “Mix them”, Apply uses the mix you previewed.\n\nSubmitted work stays put: a plot that someone chosen already submitted stays theirs and counts in their share, and one submitted by someone left out stays with them and is not shared out again. Submitted data is never lost by dividing again.",
  "divide.applyNote.short": "Submitted plots stay with their person if chosen again; submitted data is never lost.",
  "divide.previewTitle": "What each person would get",
  "divide.person": "Person",
  "divide.plots": "Plots",
  "divide.copies": "Copies to compare",
  "checks.title": "Automatic checks",
  "checks.explain": "Collect Earth Cloud can choose submitted plots for a second person to assess again, blind: nobody is told which plots are checks. Switch on one or both parts of the rule, choose who may receive checks, give a plot file a rule of its own if it needs one, and press “Save”. Plots submitted afterwards are drawn automatically; “Draw now” draws among those already submitted.\n\nEach plot drawn goes, as a copy, to someone who has not assessed it, does not hold it and has the fewest checks to do. They get it the next time they open Settings → “Project” in Collect Earth, or press “Refresh assignments” there, and then “Apply”. Only plot files divided between people can hold checks.",
  "checks.explain.short": "Submitted plots can be drawn for a second person to assess again, blind.",
  "checks.firstN": "Check the first plots each person submits",
  "checks.firstNCount": "How many first plots",
  "checks.percent": "Check a share of each person's plots",
  "checks.percentCount": "Share of the plots (%)",
  "checks.weekNote": "The share counts all of each person's submitted plots, rounded to the nearest plot (a half up): with 10 %, 5 of the 45 plots someone submitted get a check. Plots already checked count towards it, those of the first plots included. The checks are spread over the weeks of first submission (Monday to Sunday, UTC): a week with fewer checks for its plots comes first, so someone who submits only a few plots a week still gets checks. Plots are drawn in a fixed order, so drawing again never picks other plots.",
  "checks.weekNote.short": "The share counts all of each person's submitted plots; checks are spread over the weeks.",
