  "reference.title": "Reference plots",
  "reference.explain": "Reference plots are plots that a reference assessor (a coordinator or a reviewer you pick) assesses first, and that every collector also assesses as a check, without being told. Each collector's latest submitted check is compared, question by question, with the assessor's submitted first assessment: that is their accuracy.\n\nTo start, under “Add reference plots” choose a divided plot file, the reference assessor and the plots, then press “Mark as reference plots”. Figures appear once the assessor and the collectors have submitted their assessments. These checks are kept apart from the agreement figures, the differences and the review queue, so nothing is counted twice, and a reference plot is never decided.",
  "reference.explain.short": "Every collector also assesses these plots; their answers are compared with a reference assessment.",
  "reference.reviewerExplain": "How closely the collectors' answers on the reference plots match the reference assessments, question by question, all collectors together. Two answers match when they are the same choice, or numbers within the question's margin.\n\nAs a reviewer you see these figures per question only: no one's accuracy by name and no list of the reference plots. The coordinators choose the reference plots and their reference assessor; when they upload reference answers from a file, you also see its figures per question here.",
  "reference.reviewerExplain.short": "How closely each collector's answers match the reference assessments.",
  "reference.blind": "Collectors are not told which plots are reference plots: the plots reach them in their plot file like any other, after “Refresh assignments” (Settings → “Project”) and “Apply” in Collect Earth. This accuracy is not on their My work page nor in their report, and reviewers find no reference plot on the map or in the plot search.\n\nCollectors who compare their plot files with each other can still notice plots they all have. Picking at random makes this harder: it prefers plots whose collector has not downloaded plots yet, and spreads the picks over the file instead of taking neighbouring plots.",
  "reference.blind.short": "Collectors are not told which plots are reference plots, nor shown this accuracy.",
  "reference.none": "No reference plots yet.",
  "reference.count": "Reference plots: {count} (at most {max})",
  "reference.addTitle": "Add reference plots",
  "reference.file": "Plot file",
  "reference.assessor": "Reference assessor",
  "reference.assessorHelp": "They get these plots as their own: their first assessment is the reference. A coordinator or a reviewer.",
  "reference.assessorHelp.more": "The reference assessor holds each reference plot as their own plot; a collector who was dealt it keeps it only as a check copy. The assessor's latest submitted first assessment is the reference. Nothing is measured on a plot until they submit it: the “Reference assessment” column of the list shows which plots are still waiting. A plot that someone else has already assessed first cannot be marked.",
  "reference.how": "Which plots",
  "reference.howRandom": "Pick them at random among the plots nobody has started",
  "reference.howList": "These plot ids",
  "reference.randomCount": "How many plots",
  "reference.plotIds": "Plot ids, one per line",
  "reference.plotIdsHelp": "Type or paste the plot ids as they are in the plot file, for example lagoon, one per line; a column pasted from a spreadsheet works too (tabs and semicolons also separate ids). When plots have several key columns, type the keys separated by commas (lagoon,1); the first key alone is enough when only one plot has it.\n\nAt most 500 ids at a time. If an id is not in this file, is also in another plot file, or was already assessed first by someone other than the reference assessor, nothing is marked and the message names those plots.",
  "reference.plotIdsHelp.short": "The id as in the plot file, for example lagoon; with several key columns: lagoon,1.",
  "reference.add": "Mark as reference plots",
  "reference.added": "Reference plots added: {count}. Each collector gets them the next time they press “Refresh assignments” in Collect Earth (Settings → “Project”) and then “Apply”.",
  "reference.wholeFiles": "Plot files given whole cannot hold reference plots; give their plots one by one (divide them) first: {files}.",
  "reference.noDivided": "No plot file is divided yet. Reference plots are plots of a plot file whose plots are given one by one.",
  "reference.collectors": "Every collector gets each reference plot as an extra plot in their plot file (collectors now: {count}), so each reference plot adds one assessment to every collector's work. Reviewers, coordinators and the reference assessor get no copy.\n\nSomeone who joins later gets them on their next “Refresh assignments”. Someone whose account is disabled, or who is no longer a collector, loses the copies they have not started.",
  "reference.collectors.short": "Every collector gets each reference plot (collectors now: {count}).",
