  "reference.removed": "Reference plots removed: {count}.",
  "reference.waitingNote": "Only plots whose reference assessment is submitted are measured ({assessed} of {plots}).",
  "reference.accuracyTitle": "Accuracy against the reference",
  "reference.accuracyExplain": "For each person, lowest first: the share of their measured reference plots where every answer matched the reference (the same choice, or numbers within the margin set under “Margins for numbers”). One differing answer makes the whole plot a miss, so this share is usually lower than the figures per question. “Differs most on” names up to three questions they missed most; the table below gives each question for everyone together.\n\nOnly each person's latest submitted check of a plot counts, and only once its reference assessment is submitted. A share is shown from 20 plots; below that it says there are too few to judge. Assessments measured: {checks}.",
  "reference.accuracyExplain.short": "Per person: plots matching the reference in every answer. Assessments measured: {checks}.",
  "reference.accuracyExplainQuestions": "By question, all collectors' checks of the reference plots together: how often the answer matches the reference assessment (the same choice, or numbers within the question's margin). A question left blank on both sides is not counted. The questions are in the survey's order.\n\nOnly each person's latest submitted check of a plot counts, and only once its reference assessment is submitted. A share is shown from 20 compared answers; below that it says there are too few to judge. Assessments measured: {checks}.",
  "reference.accuracyExplainQuestions.short": "By question: how often the answers match the reference. Assessments measured: {checks}.",
