  "data.title": "Collected data",
  "data.explain": "Download everything collected so far as one file that opens in Excel or any spreadsheet program: one line for each plot and person.",
  "data.explain.more": "One line for each plot and person who saved it, submitted or not; deleted records are left out. The first columns give the plot and round; assessment (main for a first assessment, check for a quality check); final, from the decisions on the Quality tab (yes for the answers taken, no for the others, recheck for “Both need another look”, blank without a decision); reference (yes for a reference plot); operator; actively_saved (true once submitted); modified_on, in UTC. One column per answer follows.\n\nThe records of people left out of the results are in it only if you tick the box to include them, offered when someone is left out. Each download is noted in the Activity tab.",
  "data.summary": "Plots submitted: {submitted}. Plots saved in all: {total}.",
  "data.empty": "No data yet. When people submit plots in Collect Earth, they appear here.",
  "data.download": "Download the data",
  "data.downloading": "Preparing the file…",
  "data.downloaded": "The file was downloaded. Look in your Downloads folder.",
  "data.format": "File type",
  "data.formatCsv": "Spreadsheet (CSV)",
  "data.formatGeojson": "Map: GeoJSON",
  "data.formatKml": "Map: KML (Google Earth)",
  "data.formatShp": "Map: shapefile (zip)",
  "data.formatHint": "The map files (GeoJSON; KML, which opens in Google Earth; a zipped shapefile) have one item for each line of the spreadsheet, with the same columns. Each plot is drawn with the survey's plot shape, a square or a circle of its size, in latitude and longitude (WGS84); when the shape is not known the plot is a point, and a plot whose place is not known has no shape.\n\nA shapefile's column names are at most 10 characters and it holds at most 255 columns: fields.csv in the zip gives the full column name of each field, and lists any column left out. “Leave out where the plots are” is offered for the spreadsheet only: a map file always has the plots' places.",
  "data.formatHint.short": "Map files draw each plot with the survey's plot shape and have the spreadsheet's columns.",
  "data.checkTitle": "Quality check",
  "data.checkMoved": "The comparison of first assessments and quality checks is now in the Quality tab, with the figures by question, person and week.",
  "data.checkOpen": "Open the Quality tab",
  "analysis.title": "Analyse the data",
  "analysis.open": "Open the analysis",
  "analysis.cardText": "Count plots and add up areas by any question of the survey, in a table or a chart, as Saiku did, for any survey. The data is loaded into this browser when the analysis opens, so nothing is installed; open it again to see the plots saved since.\n\nPick what to count in “Show”, the questions in “By (rows)” and “And by (columns)”, and keep only some values with “Add a filter”; click a cell to list its plots. “Save the view” keeps a view in this browser; “Share with the team” gives it to everyone in the project. Reviewers see every plot of the project there too; collectors see only their own.",
  "analysis.cardText.short": "Count plots and add up areas by any question of the survey, in a table or a chart.",
