  "analysis.empty": "No data yet. When people save plots in Collect Earth, you can analyse them here.",
  "analysis.emptyOwn": "You have not saved any plot yet. When you do, you can analyse your plots here.",
  "analysis.explain": "All the plots saved in this project ({count} records: one for each plot and person), first assessments and quality checks, submitted or not. Deleted records are left out; the records of people left out of the results are in. The view starts with the first assessments only, as the checks are other people's answers for the same plots: remove the filter on “Assessment” to see the checks too, or add a filter on “Submitted” to count submitted plots only.\n\nThe figures are those of when the page was opened: open it again to see the plots saved since.",
  "analysis.explain.short": "All the plots saved in this project ({count} records). The view starts with first assessments only.",
  "analysis.explainOwn": "Your own plots ({count} records).",
  "analysis.noAreas": "The project file has no areas file (region_areas.csv or areas_per_attribute.csv), so there is no Area column: the plots can be counted but not turned into hectares. With region_areas.csv (region, plot file, area), each line's area is shared equally among the plots whose region or plot file is the line's, plots of no data keeping their share too; with areas_per_attribute.csv (the questions' names, then area and optionally weight), among the plots whose answers are the line's. Only submitted first assessments count.\n\nTo get the Area column, add one of these files to the project file, upload it again on the Project file tab, and open the analysis again.",
  "analysis.noAreas.short": "The project file has no areas file: the plots can be counted but not turned into hectares.",
