  "backup.title": "Collect Earth backup",
  "backup.explain": "One zip file that Collect Earth imports: the survey of the project file and the records, each exactly as the person's Collect Earth sent it, with all its answers. Keep it as a backup, or import it in Collect Earth to use its IPCC and Saiku exports.\n\n“Download a Collect Earth backup…” first shows how many records the file will hold and what is left out. Choose the first assessments only or all rounds, then press “Download the backup”: your browser downloads the file by itself and shows its progress. Deleted records are not in it; the records of people left out of the results are. The server prepares one backup at a time, and each download is noted in the Activity tab.",
  "backup.explain.short": "The survey and all records in one file that Collect Earth imports: a backup, or for its exports.",
  "backup.open": "Download a Collect Earth backup…",
  "backup.dialogTitle": "Download a Collect Earth backup",
  "backup.which": "Which records",
  "backup.first": "First assessments only",
  "backup.firstHelp": "One record for each plot, its first assessment. When a plot has more than one, the file keeps the one of the person who holds the plot now, else a submitted one, else the one saved last. Quality checks are left out, and so are the collectors' measurements of reference plots; the reference assessment itself is in.\n\nRecords saved but not submitted are in it: the list below counts them, and Collect Earth asks when importing whether to take them too.",
  "backup.firstHelp.short": "One record for each plot. Quality checks are left out.",
  "backup.all": "All rounds: first assessments and quality checks",
  "backup.allHelp": "Quality checks go in as round 2, beside the first assessments. Collect Earth's IPCC exports count round 1 only.",
  "backup.noRoundKey": "Your survey has no 'round' key, so a plot's first assessment and its quality check have the same key, and Collect Earth keeps one record per key: only the first assessments can be in the backup, and “All rounds” cannot be chosen. The quality checks are not lost: the data download (CSV) above has them, each on its own line with its round.",
  "backup.noRoundKey.short": "Your survey has no 'round' key, so only the first assessments can be in the backup.",
  "backup.noProjectFile": "Upload a project file first: the backup carries its survey.",
  "backup.records": "Records in the file: {count}.",
  "backup.drafts": "Of them, saved but not submitted: {count}. When importing, Collect Earth asks whether to import these too.",
  "backup.otherRounds": "Quality checks left out: {count}.",
  "backup.sameKey": "Left out because another record has the same plot and round: {count} (for example {examples}). This happens when more than one person saved the same plot in the same round, such as two first assessments of one plot. Collect Earth keeps one record per plot and round, so the file has the one of the person who holds the plot now, else the submitted one, else the one saved last.\n\nThe data download (CSV) has them all, one line for each person. Plots with more than one first assessment are also listed under Data problems on the Quality tab.",
  "backup.sameKey.short": "Left out because another record has the same plot and round: {count} (for example {examples}).",
  "backup.note": "Each record keeps the coordinator's note it was saved with: the comment the person saw at the top of the form.",
  "backup.howTo": "To import it, open this project in Collect Earth with the project file from this server (the import looks for the same survey), choose Data Import/Export → Import data (ZIP or CSV) → “Records from a Collect Earth export (ZIP with XML)”, and pick the file. Records of plots that Collect Earth already has are shown as conflicts, and it asks whether to replace them; it also asks whether to import the records saved but not submitted.",
  "backup.howTo.short": "To import it in Collect Earth: Data Import/Export → Import data (ZIP or CSV).",
  "backup.clientMode": "That menu entry is not shown when Collect Earth works with another computer's database (client mode): import the file on the computer that keeps the database.",
  "backup.started": "The download has started: your browser shows its progress and saves the file in your Downloads folder.",
  "import.title": "Import data from Collect Earth",
  "import.explain.short": "The records collected in Collect Earth before the project moved to the cloud become the project's records.",
  "import.explain": "In Collect Earth, choose Data Import/Export > Export data with the format “XML (compressed, to share with other Collect Earth installations)”, and drop that file here. It must be of this project's survey. You first see what the file holds: nothing is stored until you press Import. Each record keeps the person who collected it and whether it was submitted. When the project already has a newer version of a record, the newer one stays. The import is noted in the Activity tab.",
  "import.desktop": "Each person can also send their records from Collect Earth itself, with Data Import/Export > Send this computer's records to the cloud project.",
  "import.drop": "Drag the Collect Earth export (.zip) here",
  "import.choose": "Choose the file",
  "import.reading": "Reading the file…",
  "import.summary": "Records in the file: {records} ({submitted} submitted, {drafts} not submitted).",
  "import.new": "New to the project: {count}.",
  "import.older": "Replacing an older version in the project: {count}.",
  "import.newer": "Already newer in the project, so left as they are: {count}.",
  "import.problems": "Files that could not be read: {count}.",
  "import.people": "People in the file",
