  "settings.aiTitle": "AI assistant",
  "settings.aiSwitch": "Use the AI assistant in this project",
  "settings.aiIntro": "On the Quality tab, the assistant (Google's Gemini model) reads the quality figures and points out what to look at: questions that get mixed up, habits of one person, plots to check again. It can draft a guidance note, which opens for you to edit and save, but it never changes anything itself. It stays off until a coordinator switches it on here, and only coordinators can use it.\n\nWhen you switch it on, a window first shows what is sent and where, and asks you to confirm that the project's agreements allow it. You can switch it off at any time; earlier reviews stay listed on the Quality tab. Each project may make a set number of reviews and questions a day, and use a set amount a month, as the server owner decides. Switching it on or off is noted on the Activity tab.",
  "settings.aiIntro.short": "On the Quality tab, the assistant (Gemini) suggests guidance notes and plots to check again.",
  "settings.aiSent": "What is sent: the project's quality figures, the answers to choice and number questions, the survey's questions, answer options and help texts, and your guidance notes. People's names are replaced by “Person A”, “Person B” and plot ids by “Plot 1”, “Plot 2”, and a username written in your texts is replaced too; the dashboard shows the real ones again in the result. Coordinates (and number questions named like them), comments, other text answers and answers that are not in the question's list are never sent.",
  "settings.aiSent.short": "Only choice and number answers, the survey and your notes are sent, with names hidden.",
  "settings.aiSentViews": "On the analysis page, \"Ask AI for more views\" sends only the survey's structure (its questions, code lists and labels): never a plot, an answer or a person.",
  "settings.aiWhere": "Processed by {provider} ({model}), in the region {region}.",
  "settings.aiWhereGlobal": "Processed by {provider} ({model}). Its region is \"global\": Google may process it in any of its regions. The server's owner can fix one region (AI_VERTEX_REGION): ask them before switching it on if the project's agreements require the data to stay in a given region.",
  "settings.aiWhereGlobal.short": "Processed by {provider} ({model}), in any of Google's regions.",
  "settings.aiConfirmTitle": "Switch the AI assistant on?",
  "settings.aiConfirmTerms": "Before switching it on, check that sending these data to this provider is allowed by the agreements of this project (with the data's owner, and the country's rules), and by the provider's terms, which the server's owner accepted.",
  "settings.aiConfirmCheck": "I have checked: these data may be sent for this project",
  "settings.aiConfirmOn": "Switch it on",
  "settings.aiNotAvailable": "Not available on this server: the server owner has not set it up or switched it on.",
  "settings.aiOn": "The AI assistant is on for this project.",
  "settings.aiOff": "The AI assistant is off for this project.",
  "server.aiTitle": "AI assistant",
  "server.aiIntro": "Coordinators can ask an AI assistant (Gemini on Vertex AI) to review their project's quality figures. Each use is billed to this server's Google Cloud account. Each project also has its own switch, off by default.",
  "server.aiIntro.short": "An AI assistant reviews a project's quality figures, billed to this server's Google Cloud.",
  "server.aiEnabled": "Allow the AI assistant on this server",
  "server.aiNotSetUp": "Not set up on this server.",
  "server.aiNotSetUpHelp": "The server needs its Vertex AI settings first (see the AI assistant section of DEPLOY.md).",
  "server.aiEnabledHelp": "Coordinators then switch it on for their own project.",
  "server.aiLimitsIntro": "Each limit counts per project. 0 allows none.",
  "server.aiReports": "AI reviews per project per day",
  "server.aiReportsHelp": "Reviews that finished. A day ends at midnight UTC. At most {max}.",
  "server.aiFollowUps": "Follow-ups and questions per project per day",
