  "myWork.link": "My work",
  "myWork.title": "My work",
  "myWork.coordinatorsSee": "Coordinators of this project see when and how much you work, your answers, and quality figures about your work. Reviewers, who also collect plots, see the answers of the plots they review and who made them. This page shows your own numbers.",
  "myWork.coordinatorsSee.short": "Coordinators see when and how much you work, your answers and quality figures about your work.",
  "peopleWeek.title": "This week",
  "peopleWeek.explain": "Plots first submitted in the last 7 days, today included: {n} in all. Each column is a day, today on the right; a plot counts on the day its first assessment was first submitted, and quality checks are not counted. Days are those of your time zone, {zone}. Point at a column, or select the chart and use the arrow keys, to read its figure; “Table” lists the days.\n\n“Most active” names up to 3 people with the most plots submitted in these days. “Least active” names up to 3 people who still have plots or checks to do and submitted the fewest, none included; nobody is in both lists. Click a name to open that person's page, for example to see when they last synced.",
  "peopleWeek.explain.short": "Plots first submitted in the last 7 days, today included: {n} in all.",
  "peopleWeek.most": "Most active",
  "peopleWeek.least": "Least active",
  "peopleWeek.leastHelp": "Among the people with plots left to do.",
  "peopleWeek.nobody": "Nobody submitted plots in these days.",
  "peopleWeek.nobodyLeft": "Nobody else has plots left to do.",
  "peopleTable.title": "How each person is doing",
  "peopleTable.explain": "One row per person. “Plots done” counts the plots they hold that are submitted, as on the Progress tab: a plot is done once its first assessment is submitted, by them or by someone else; the quality checks they hold are counted apart, under it.\n\nThe status comes from their last sync or plot download: someone with plots left is quiet after more than {days} days without either (red after twice that), and “Never started” has plots and has sent nothing yet. The number of days is set on the Settings tab (“Quiet after this many days”). The table starts with the most worrying status; click a heading to sort by it, again to reverse. “Download as CSV” gives everyone, sorted by name, whatever the search or filter. Times are those of your time zone, {zone}; point at a time to see the exact date.",
  "peopleTable.explain.short": "One row per person. Plots are counted as on the Progress tab.",
