  "peopleTable.agreementNotYet": "Agreement shows “—” until the quality figures have been worked out: open the Quality tab once.",
  "peopleTable.footnote": "Agreement: of the quality checks made of plots this person assessed first, the share that agreed with their answers on every compared question. It is given from 20 checks on; with fewer, the column says how many so far. “—” means none yet, or that the quality figures have not been worked out (open the Quality tab). A difference does not say who was wrong: look at the plots on the Quality tab before talking to someone.\n\nPlots a day (“usually … a day”): the median over the days they submitted at least one plot. Days without plots are left out, so it is their pace on the days they work, not how often they work; quality checks are not counted.",
  "peopleTable.footnote.short": "Agreement needs at least 20 checked plots; plots a day is a median.",
