  "person.activityTitle": "Days and hours of work",
  "person.calendarTitle": "Plots submitted each day",
  "person.calendarExplain": "Each square is a day, one column per week with Monday at the top, from their first day with a submission (at most a year back) to today, which has an outline. The darker the square, the more plots and checks were first submitted that day, in four steps up to their busiest day; the palest means none. It shows the days worked, not the hours: those are under “Hours of the day”.\n\nPoint at a square, or select the calendar and use the arrow keys, to read the day's figures; “Table” lists every day with a submission. Days are those of your time zone, {zone}.",
  "person.calendarExplain.short": "Each square is a day: the darker, the more plots and checks were submitted.",
