  "person.role": "Role",
  "person.newLink": "Make a link for the new project file",
  "person.newLinkHelp": "Collect Earth downloads the project file only when joining, so someone already in the project keeps the old one after you replace it; this page warns when their copy is old. “Make a link for the new project file” makes a link for this person only: send it to them. In Collect Earth they choose File → Join cloud project..., paste it, then “Log in” with their account (not Register): they get the project file as it is now.\n\nLogging in does not use the link up and their role does not change. It works for a week and is listed under “Invitation links still open”, where you can stop it earlier. Anyone else who opened it would join as a collector, so send it to them only.",
  "person.newLinkHelp.short": "A new link gives them the project file as it is now. It works for a week.",
  "person.newLinkReady": "Send it to {name} only: for safety it is shown only once. They press “Log in” in Collect Earth, not Register.",
  "person.removePlots": "{n} plots that only they hold are not submitted yet: once they are removed, those plots are given to nobody. Move them to someone else first, on this page.",
  "answers.title": "Answers per person",
  "answers.datesOrder": "The first day is after the last one: the dates are not applied until they are in order.",
  "answers.noAnswers": "No answers",
  "answers.flagsCount": "{n} found in {tests} comparisons of a person with the rest of the team.",
  "answers.chanceNone": "Chance alone would hardly ever give even one.",
  "answers.chance": "Chance alone would give about {n} of them.",
  "answers.blankFiltered": "{n} plots in the filters have no answer to it.",
  "answers.blankFilteredOne": "{n} plot in the filters has no answer to it.",
  "answers.explain": "How each person answers the questions, from the first assessments of the plots (quality checks are not counted). Pick a question to see, for a choice, the share of the plots giving each answer and, for a number, how the numbers spread; with a person chosen, their figures are set against the rest of the team. The filters narrow the plots by plot file, by a value of a column of the plot file, or by the days they were saved.\n\nAn answer someone gives much more or much less often than the rest of the team is listed under “Worth a look”: their plots may be different, or they may read the question another way. “Show” opens that question for that person. Nothing is blocked or changed.",
  "answers.explain.short": "How each person answers, from first assessments; unusual answers are listed as worth a look.",
  "answers.explainTeam": "How the team answers the questions, from the first assessments of the plots (quality checks are not counted): for a choice, the share of the plots giving each answer; for a number, how the numbers spread. As a reviewer you see the team's figures only: each person's answers are for the coordinators. The filters (plot file, a value of a column, the days saved) must keep at least 5 plots from at least 2 people, and values held by fewer than 5 plots are not offered.",
  "answers.explainTeam.short": "How the team answers the questions, from the first assessments of the plots.",
  "answers.tooFewPlots": "This filter holds fewer than 5 plots, or one person's plots only. Reviewers see the team's answers only for groups of at least 5 plots from at least 2 people (otherwise the answers would be one person's), and the Value menu offers no value held by fewer than 5 plots. Choose a larger plot file, value or period, or press “Clear the filters” to go back to all the plots.",
  "answers.tooFewPlots.short": "Fewer than 5 plots, or one person's only: choose a larger filter or clear the filters.",
