  "answers.flagsTitle": "Worth a look",
  "answers.flagsExplain": "Someone with at least 20 plots answering a choice question, who gives an answer at least 10 points more or less often than the rest of the team (who also need 20 plots answering it), a difference larger than chance usually makes: chance alone reaches it in about 3 of 1,000 comparisons. Answers too rare to compare fairly are left out. When some are found, the line above the list says how many comparisons were made and about how many flags chance alone would give.\n\nWith many people and questions some of these are still chance, and plots in different areas can differ: look at the plots before judging. “Show” opens the question for that person. The dates are the day each plot was last saved, in your time zone.",
