  "quality.reviewerNote": "As a reviewer you work the review queue here (your decisions are kept with your name) and see the plots worth a look, the team's answers, the survey health and the accuracy against the reference plots; the rest of the Quality tab is the coordinators'.",
  "quality.reviewerNote.short": "As a reviewer you work the review queue here; your decisions are kept with your name.",
  "flags.title": "Plots worth a look",
  "flags.explain": "Plots found from how they were collected, without any quality check: submitted very quickly after the same person's plot before (under the threshold shown here, 15 seconds unless a coordinator changes it), with every answer the same as on their plot before (3 or more plots in a row), with a required answer left empty, saved again after a decision, with more than one first assessment, or in no plot file. None of them is surely a mistake, and nothing is blocked or changed: open the plot and judge for yourself.\n\nThe Kind menu (and, for coordinators, Person and “By person”) narrows the list. Plots without a decision also wait in the review queue, where deciding takes them out.",
  "flags.explain.short": "Plots worth a look from how they were collected. None is surely a mistake: open it and judge.",
  "flags.requiredNote": "Only questions the survey requires whatever the other answers are counted as required. A question required only under a condition, or shown only under one, cannot be judged here, so it is never counted. Each plot found names the questions left empty.",
