  "shareLinks.title": "Progress links for funders",
  "shareLinks.intro": "A progress link opens a page, with no login, that shows this project's name, how many plots are done, the progress chart, the forecast (from the deadline and target set above) and the quality agreement as one figure. The figures are worked out each time the page is opened, but the quality figure is the one from the last time the quality figures were worked out, with its time.\n\nType a note (who the link is for, say) and press “Make a link”, then copy the address: it is shown only this once. Make one link per funder, so each can be revoked alone; the list shows when each was last opened. A project can have up to 20 links. Anyone who has a link can open the page until you revoke it, also after the project is closed. Revoking cannot be undone, but you can make a new link. A printed or saved copy of the page may carry the link's address, so share those with the same care.",
  "shareLinks.intro.short": "A link to a page, with no login, that shows this project's progress until you revoke the link.",
  "shareLinks.never": "The page never shows people's names, answers, plot ids, file names or where the plots are, nor anyone's own counts, and your note is not shown either. In a small team, though, the daily chart shows when the work was done. Search engines are asked not to list the page, and browsers not to keep a copy of it.",
  "shareLinks.never.short": "The page never shows people's names, answers, plot ids or where the plots are.",
  "shareLinks.logs": "Whoever can read this server's request logs can see the links too.",
  "shareLinks.label": "Note to tell links apart",
  "shareLinks.labelExample": "For the donor",
  "shareLinks.labelHelp": "Only coordinators see it, not the people who open the link.",
  "shareLinks.create": "Make a link",
  "shareLinks.copyOnce": "The link is ready. Copy it now: for safety it is shown only this once. If you lose it, revoke it and make another one.",
  "shareLinks.noLabel": "Progress link (no note)",
